The Lua implementation of {{Tl|Reprint}}, [[Module:Reprint]] and its [[Module:Reprint/data]] dataset are responsible for generating {{C|reprinted in ''Other Media Title''}} after an Appearance or Source, without needing to manually specify in ''which'' media it's been reprinted. It works like the [[Module:ArchiveAccess|ArchiveAccess]] system, using the media name provided in the Reprint template to look up the reprints for that title in the dataset on the Module:Reprint/data page. It has some custom logic around the [[Star Wars (1977)|''Star Wars'' (1977)]] series and can abbreviate some titles based on the <code>abbr=</code> parameter, but most of the time, any changes needed will be made to the dataset.

The dataset has two sections: the <code>formatting</code> map at the start, which is a Lua map of title/formatted-title pairs, and then the rest of the dataset, which is each title and their reprints. Reprints for a given title are listed in the <code>issues</code> list for that title. The <code>color</code> boolean value denotes a colorized reprint, and the <code>format</code> value denotes special cases where the full formatted links are specified in their own array for edge cases.